  faqs: { en: [
    { q: "How long does a Tradovate transfer stay pending?", a: "Deposits typically clear in one to two business days, and ACH deposits beat the same-day cutoff if you request them before roughly 1:30 PM Central. Withdrawals process the same business day when you submit them before noon Central; otherwise they move to the next day. A locked ACH deposit is the exception, plan on about three business days there." },
    { q: "Why does my ACH deposit say locked instead of pending?", a: "A lock happens when Tradovate's bank-verification partner can't confirm your balance at the moment of deposit. Because an ACH transfer can be clawed back for insufficient funds, the deposit is held for about three business days before it's usable. Nothing's wrong on your end, and the hold can't be sped up." },
    { q: "Can I see transfer status on the mobile app?", a: "Transfer History lives in the web app, so log in through a browser to view your full deposit and withdrawal record. And remember: prop-firm evaluation and funded accounts track payouts through the firm's own process, not this page. Firm payout rules and timing vary by firm and account size, so check your firm's current terms." },
